910</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Diaz, L., P. Meera, J. Amigo, E. Stefani, O. Alvarez, L. Toro, and R. Latorre. <year>1998</year>. Role of the S4 segment in a voltage- dependent calcium-sensitive potassium (hSlo) channel. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>273</volume>:<fpage>32430</fpage>&#x02013;32436.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9829973</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Dong, J., N. Shi, I. Berke, L. Chen, and Y. Jiang. <year>2005</year>. Structures of the MTHK RCK domain and the effect of Ca<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup> on gating ring stability. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>280</volume>:<fpage>41716</fpage>&#x02013;41724.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16227203</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Doyle, D.A., C.J. Morais, R.A. Pfuetzner, A. Kuo, J.M. Gulbis, S.L. Cohen, B.T. Chait, and R. Mackinnon. <year>1998</year>. The structure of the potassium channel: molecular basis of K<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> conduction and selectivity. <source>Science.</source> <volume>280</volume>:<fpage>69</fpage>&#x02013;77.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9525859</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Golowasch, J., A. Kirkwood, and C. Miller. <year>1986</year>. Allosteric effects of Mg<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup> on the gating of Ca<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup>-activated K<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> channels from mammalian skeletal muscle. <source>J. Exp. Biol.</source> <volume>124</volume>:<fpage>5</fpage>&#x02013;13.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2428908</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Hamill, O.P., A. Marty, E. Neher, B. Sakmann, and F.J. Sigworth. <year>1981</year>. Improved patch-clamp techniques for high-resolution current recording from cells and cell-free membrane patches. <source>Pflugers Arch.</source> <volume>391</volume>:<fpage>85</fpage>&#x02013;100.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6270629</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Horrigan, F.T., and R.W. Aldrich. <year>1999</year>. Allosteric voltage gating of potassium channels II. Mslo channel gating charge movement in the absence of Ca<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup>. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>114</volume>:<fpage>305</fpage>&#x02013;336.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10436004</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Horrigan, F.T., and R.W. Aldrich. <year>2002</year>. Coupling between voltage sensor activation, Ca<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup> binding and channel opening in large conductance (BK) potassium channels. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>120</volume>:<fpage>267</fpage>&#x02013;305.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12198087</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Horrigan, F.T., J. Cui, and R.W. Aldrich. <year>1999</year>. Allosteric voltage gating of potassium channels I. Mslo ionic currents in the absence of Ca<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup>. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>114</volume>:<fpage>277</fpage>&#x02013;304.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10436003</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Horrigan, F.T., S.H. Heinemann, and T. Hoshi. <year>2005</year>. Heme regulates allosteric activation of the Slo1 BK channel. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>126</volume>:<fpage>7</fpage>&#x02013;21.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15955873</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Hu, L., J. Shi, Z. Ma, G. Krishnamoorthy, F. Sieling, G. Zhang, F.T. Horrigan, and J. Cui. <year>2003</year>. Participation of the S4 voltage sensor in the Mg<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup>-dependent activation of large conductance (BK) K<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> channels. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>100</volume>:<fpage>10488</fpage>&#x02013;10493.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12925732</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Jiang,